--TEST--
Core\Crypto::generateKeyPair draws the three kinds of the roster that are drawn and refuses both RSA kinds with one LogicError naming the member that reads one — `rule:core-classes/crypto-interop-tier`, `rule:security/algorithm-comes-from-the-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Crypto\KeyKind
//
// The bound named on both sides: every case of `Core\Crypto\KeyKind` is asked
// for, and each one either draws a pair or is the refusal. A member that had
// grown a sixth kind, or lost one of the three, fails here while looking right
// on whichever line it kept.
array<Core\Crypto\KeyKind> $drawn = [
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::P256,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::X25519,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::Ed25519,
];
array<Core\Crypto\KeyKind> $issued = [
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::RsaPkcs1,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::RsaPss,
];

int $pairs = 0;
foreach (Core\Arr::range(0, 2) as int $slot) {
    Core\Crypto\KeyPair $pair = Core\Crypto::generateKeyPair($drawn[$slot]);
    if ($pair->publicKey()->kind() == $drawn[$slot]) {
        $pairs += 1;
    }
}
echo "drawn ", $pairs, " of ", Core\Arr::count($drawn), "\n";

// An RSA key is never generated: `ring` generates none, and a program is handed
// its RSA key by whoever issued it. So this is a `LogicError` — a bug in the
// call and not a verdict on anything — and its sentence names
// `Core\Crypto\KeyPair::read`, which is the member that does take the file.
array<string> $said = [];
foreach (Core\Arr::range(0, 1) as int $slot) {
    try {
        Core\Crypto\KeyPair $never = Core\Crypto::generateKeyPair($issued[$slot]);
        echo "an RSA kind was drawn", "\n";
    } catch (LogicError $bug) {
        $said = Core\Arr::append($said, $bug->message);
    }
}
echo "refused ", Core\Arr::count($said), " of ", Core\Arr::count($issued), "\n";

int $oneSentence = 0;
foreach ($said as string $message) {
    if ($message == $said[0]) {
        $oneSentence += 1;
    }
}
echo "one sentence ", $oneSentence, " of ", Core\Arr::count($said), "\n";
echo $said[0], "\n";
--EXPECT--
drawn 3 of 3
refused 2 of 2
one sentence 2 of 2
Core\Crypto::generateKeyPair(): an RSA key is never generated here. A program is handed its RSA key by whoever issued it, so read that file with `Core\Crypto\KeyPair::read`.
